# Copy this to .env, which is gitignored. Nothing here is required — every
# target that needs one of these checks for it and says so.
#
# Read by make rather than sourced by a shell, which changes the rules: plain
# KEY=value, no `export`, no quotes around the value, and a `#` anywhere on a
# line starts a comment. A token with a `#` in it would need another home;
# GitHub's and noeto's do not have one.

# A classic GitHub token, for `make release`: it creates the release on this
# repo and commits the Homebrew cask to noeto-tasks/homebrew-tap, which is why
# the scope has to be `repo` whole rather than a fine-grained grant on one of
# them. Give it `write:packages` as well and the same token is the one you hand
# to `docker login ghcr.io` for `make docker-push` — that login is Docker's own
# credential store, so it is typed once and not read from here.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...

# A noeto access token, for `make smoke` — the contract check that runs against
# a real API, since nothing else in this repo would notice noeto renaming a
# field. Issue it in the app under Settings → Access tokens; it is bound to the
# team you were in when you created it.
#
# Point it at a team whose board you do not mind being read. The check only
# reads, but it reads whatever is there.
# NOETO_TOKEN=noeto_pat_...

# Where `make smoke` looks for that API. Defaults to a local noeto on 8081, so
# this only matters when checking against a deployed one.
# NOETO_API_URL=http://localhost:8081/api/v1
